WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:49.375


2
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:51.625
<b>Seeing his teachers, loved ones, </b>

3
00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:56.916
<b>and close relatives thus divided into</b>
<b>two factions on the battlefield, </b>

4
00:00:56.916 --> 00:00:59.500
<b>Arjuna was filled with compassion.</b>

5
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.166
<b>He says to Lord Krishna,</b>

6
00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:10.833
<b>"O Krishna, seeing my own people here,</b>

7
00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:14.583
<b>I feel trembling throughout my entire body,</b>

8
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:18.500
<b>I'm getting chills all over, my skin is burning</b>

9
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:24.416
<b>Even my Gandiva bow is slipping from my hand,</b>
<b>O Krishna."</b>

10
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.291


11
00:01:29.291 --> 00:01:31.125
<b>Arjuna's mind and body</b>

12
00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:33.625
<b>have suddenly become unstable.</b>

13
00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:36.083
<b>His hands are shaking,</b>

14
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:38.333
<b>his mouth is drying up,</b>

15
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.916
<b>and his bow is slipping from his hands.</b>

16
00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:44.375
<b>Distress has engulfed him from all sides.</b>

17
00:01:44.375 --> 00:01:50.000
<b>He is openly expressing his helpless state to</b>
<b>Lord Krishna, as if pleading, </b>

18
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.791
<b>"O Krishna, you have taken charge of my chariot,</b>

19
00:01:53.791 --> 00:01:55.333
<b>please take charge of me too,</b>

20
00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:58.166
<b>otherwise I will break down and fall."</b>

21
00:01:58.166 --> 00:02:02.208
<b>And this is where Arjuna's sorrow begins, </b>

22
00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:03.583
<b>his despair,</b>

23
00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:09.458
<b>the scorching fire of questions and dilemmas</b>

24
00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:12.083
<b>And to quench this fire,</b>

25
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:15.416
<b>the nectar of the Bhagavad Gita will pour down, </b>

26
00:02:15.416 --> 00:02:23.125
<b>each verse of which will cool down</b>
<b>every mind like pure, cold water.</b>

27
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.833
<b>Lord Krishna is the master of this universe,</b>

28
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:26.750
<b>omniscient.</b>

29
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.291
<b>His becoming Arjuna's charioteer</b>
<b>was not a coincidence.</b>

30
00:02:30.291 --> 00:02:35.916
<b>He knew that when this difficult hour</b>
<b>would come, Arjuna would need guidance. </b>

31
00:02:35.916 --> 00:02:38.208
<b>And not just Arjuna,</b>

32
00:02:38.208 --> 00:02:41.708
<b>but the entire world needs those teachings,</b>

33
00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:48.625
<b>based on which anyone can find</b>

34
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.041


35
00:02:53.041 --> 00:02:58.708
<b>The change within Arjuna here is noteworthy.</b>

36
00:02:58.708 --> 00:03:03.791
<b>Just a little while ago,</b>
<b>he had said with great pride,</b>

37
00:03:03.791 --> 00:03:06.666
<b>"I want to go to the middle of the battlefield,</b>

38
00:03:06.666 --> 00:03:12.166
<b>I want to see who is supporting</b>
<b>that wicked Duryodhana."</b>

39
00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:16.333
<b>Then, the 'I' was dominant in his voice.</b>

40
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:17.833
<b>But now? </b>

41
00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:23.208
<b>Now the burden of that same</b>
<b>'I' is weighing heavily on him, </b>

42
00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:24.916
<b>and because of this,</b>

43
00:03:24.916 --> 00:03:30.625
<b>he is unable to see his duty beyond</b>
<b>personal relationships. </b>

44
00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:35.750
<b>Arjuna is looking at every situation,</b>
<b>every person, as Arjuna,</b>

45
00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.500
<b>not as a king,</b>

46
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.125
<b>not as a warrior, </b>

47
00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:44.041
<b>and not even by looking at</b>
<b>righteousness/unrighteousness.</b>

48
00:03:44.041 --> 00:03:46.708
<b>Many such situations will come,</b>

49
00:03:46.708 --> 00:03:54.458
<b>where you too will find yourself caught</b>
<b>in such a dilemma.</b>

50
00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:56.291
<b>What will you do then?</b>

51
00:03:56.291 --> 00:03:58.958
<b>Duty!</b>

52
00:03:58.958 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>Fulfilling one's duty is the</b>
<b>right answer to this question.</b>

53
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.666
<b>Now that the war has come, </b>

54
00:04:06.666 --> 00:04:11.541
<b>what is Arjuna's duty as a warrior? </b>

55
00:04:11.541 --> 00:04:21.333
<b>What is his responsibility towards all those</b>
<b>who are ready to sacrifice their lives for him?</b>

56
00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:23.625
<b>But</b>

57
00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:28.916
<b>when there is a thick fog of </b>
<b>emotions before the eyes, </b>

58
00:04:28.916 --> 00:04:32.916
<b>duty begins to appear hazy. </b>

59
00:04:32.916 --> 00:04:39.416
<b>There is a need for a light that can</b>
<b>pierce through this fog.</b>

60
00:04:39.416 --> 00:04:41.833
<b>Come, </b>

61
00:04:41.833 --> 00:04:43.541
<b>let's hold hands,</b>

62
00:04:43.541 --> 00:04:45.250
<b>walk together, </b>

63
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.166
<b>this fog will also disperse</b>

64
00:04:47.166 --> 00:04:50.416
<b>and the light inside the mind will also shine.</b>

65
00:04:50.916 --> 00:04:55.083


66
00:04:55.083 --> 00:05:00.416
<b>Now, a question must be stirring in your mind.</b>

67
00:05:00.416 --> 00:05:05.250
<b>Is attachment to family members wrong? </b>

68
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:09.083
<b>Isn't it natural? </b>

69
00:05:09.083 --> 00:05:11.541
<b>It absolutely is. </b>

70
00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:13.000
<b>However,</b>

71
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.541
<b>when this natural attachment </b>

72
00:05:15.541 --> 00:05:21.333
<b>begins to compel us to overlook our duties,</b>
<b>stray from righteousness, </b>

73
00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:25.916
<b>and lean towards unrighteousness,</b>

74
00:05:25.916 --> 00:05:30.125
<b>it becomes necessary to keep</b>
<b>this attachment in check.</b>

75
00:05:30.125 --> 00:05:33.208
<b>Think of it this way:</b>

76
00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:36.500
<b>a river's flow is also natural,</b>

77
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:41.250
<b>but that flow has a pace, a velocity. </b>

78
00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.250
<b>As long as that velocity is controlled,</b>

79
00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:49.541
<b>the river will give life to the</b>
<b>villages and towns along its path,</b>

80
00:05:49.541 --> 00:05:51.875
<b>help irrigate fields,</b>

81
00:05:51.875 --> 00:05:57.208
<b>and quench the thirst of</b>
<b>trees, plants, and animals.</b>

82
00:05:57.208 --> 00:05:59.625
<b>But what happens</b>

83
00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:05.625
<b>when that river swells so much</b>
<b>that it loses balance?</b>

84
00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:09.750
<b>The same river will then,</b>
<b>in the form of a flood, wreak havoc </b>

85
00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:14.791
<b>and destroy those very villages and towns.</b>

86
00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:17.666
<b>Balance.</b>

87
00:06:17.666 --> 00:06:21.041
<b>Balance is the key here.</b>

88
00:06:21.041 --> 00:06:29.458
<b>Therefore, we must establish a balance between</b>
<b>our duties and our attachments.</b>

89
00:06:29.458 --> 00:06:32.500
<b>This becomes even more crucial </b>

90
00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.916
<b>when we see a loved one,</b>

91
00:06:34.916 --> 00:06:40.250
<b>ourselves, or anyone else</b>
<b>causing harm wrongfully.</b>

92
00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.750
<b>In such cases, we must stop the wrong</b>

93
00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.250
<b>and support what's right.</b>

94
00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.750
<b>Because if we don't,</b>

95
00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:52.916
<b>these small waves of unrighteousness</b>
<b>will one day become a flood, </b>

96
00:06:52.916 --> 00:06:56.375
<b>damaging the very loved one</b>

97
00:06:56.375 --> 00:07:01.416
<b>for whom we had stopped distinguishing</b>
<b>between right and wrong due to attachment.</b>

98
00:07:01.916 --> 00:07:06.083


99
00:07:06.083 --> 00:07:07.791
<b>Professional success,</b>

100
00:07:07.791 --> 00:07:08.833
<b>fame, </b>

101
00:07:08.833 --> 00:07:10.583
<b>progress.</b>

102
00:07:10.583 --> 00:07:15.541
<b>We view all these through society's</b>
<b>established standards.</b>

103
00:07:15.541 --> 00:07:19.666
<b>We look at someone else and think,</b>

104
00:07:19.666 --> 00:07:21.000
<b>"Wow,</b>

105
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.208
<b>how successful this person is,</b>

106
00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:26.000
<b>how talented,</b>

107
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.083
<b>or how beautiful."</b>

108
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:34.625
<b>Their life must be full of happiness.</b>

109
00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:36.791
<b>But</b>

110
00:07:36.791 --> 00:07:41.958
<b>do we know what's in their heart?</b>

111
00:07:41.958 --> 00:07:46.500
<b>Haven't we seen many such examples? </b>

112
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:52.666
<b>Someone whom we or the whole society</b>
<b>considers powerful and successful,</b>

113
00:07:52.666 --> 00:07:55.625
<b>but one day it suddenly comes to light </b>

114
00:07:55.625 --> 00:07:59.416
<b>that the person was broken inside,</b>

115
00:07:59.416 --> 00:08:02.958
<b>and no one had a clue.</b>

116
00:08:02.958 --> 00:08:05.750
<b>So then, what is true success,</b>

117
00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.000
<b>external</b>

118
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.583
<b>or internal?</b>

119
00:08:08.583 --> 00:08:11.208
<b>What is true beauty,</b>

120
00:08:11.208 --> 00:08:12.208
<b>external </b>

121
00:08:12.208 --> 00:08:14.708
<b>or internal?</b>

122
00:08:14.708 --> 00:08:17.291
<b>Now the question arises,</b>

123
00:08:17.291 --> 00:08:23.041
<b>should we forget about social success? </b>

124
00:08:23.041 --> 00:08:24.458
<b>No.</b>

125
00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:27.375
<b>Absolutely not.</b>

126
00:08:27.375 --> 00:08:30.750
<b>Our life is like a building </b>

127
00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:34.250
<b>that we construct brick by brick.</b>

128
00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.541
<b>Our talents,</b>

129
00:08:35.541 --> 00:08:36.708
<b>social fame, </b>

130
00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:41.250
<b> and success add beauty to that building. </b>

131
00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:47.750
<b>And there can never be anything</b>
<b>wrong with beauty.</b>

132
00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.958
<b>But what if </b>

133
00:08:49.958 --> 00:08:53.833
<b>the foundation of that building weakens? </b>

134
00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:57.125
<b>Will that building stand?</b>

135
00:08:57.125 --> 00:08:58.583
<b>No, right? </b>

136
00:08:58.583 --> 00:09:01.750
<b>The foundation is underground,</b>

137
00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:04.083
<b>and the deeper the foundation,</b>

138
00:09:04.083 --> 00:09:07.166
<b>the stronger the building.</b>

139
00:09:07.166 --> 00:09:10.000
<b>The root is also under the earth,</b>

140
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.208
<b>and the deeper the root, </b>

141
00:09:12.208 --> 00:09:14.791
<b>the stronger the tree. </b>

142
00:09:14.791 --> 00:09:19.375
<b>The depth beneath the earth provides stability.</b>

143
00:09:19.375 --> 00:09:21.500
<b>Similarly, </b>

144
00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:27.041
<b>the depth within the mind</b>
<b>is what makes life stable. </b>

145
00:09:27.041 --> 00:09:30.291
<b>To live in a building, bricks are necessary,</b>

146
00:09:30.291 --> 00:09:32.375
<b>beauty is necessary, </b>

147
00:09:32.375 --> 00:09:34.541
<b>paint is also necessary,</b>

148
00:09:34.541 --> 00:09:36.208
<b>but</b>

149
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:39.000
<b>all this will only stay, </b>

150
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.666
<b>if the foundation is strong.</b>

151
00:09:41.666 --> 00:09:44.041
<b>Train your mind;</b>

152
00:09:44.041 --> 00:09:47.333
<b>its strength is paramount.</b>

